<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caxcanes</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Caxcan people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Caxcanes were an indigenous people of what are now the Mexican states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zacatecas">Zacatecas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalisco">Jalisco</a>, in the region the Spaniards called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-galicia">New Galicia</a>. They led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mixton-war">Mixtón War</a> of 1540–1542, the largest rising against Spanish rule in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">Viceroy</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-de-mendoza">Antonio de Mendoza</a> crushed with a large army of indigenous allies. Their lands were later absorbed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>-mining frontier.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caxcanes.jpg" alt="Caxcanes" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guerra_de_juchipila.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
